 result←object origin arg;psize;isize;yr;xr
 :If 0=≢arg
     result←object ⎕VGET⊂'_origin'(0 0)
 :Else
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: origin'##.##.Error~##.##.IsNum arg←##.##.Single arg
     '∆WI RANK ERROR: origin'##.##.Error 1<≢⍴arg
     '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: origin'##.##.Error 2≠≢arg
     (psize isize)←object ⎕VGET('_size'⍬)('_imagesize'⍬) ⍝ In scale units
⍝? What if either of these is ⍬ (undefined)?
     object._origin←arg←0⌈arg⌊isize-psize ⍝ Don't overflow, and don't complain
⍝? Don't forget to adjust imagesize and origin when changing scales
     arg←⌊0.5+arg×⊃##._supp.MyUnits object ⍝ Convert to pixels
     (yr xr)←object ##.##.∆WG'YRange' 'XRange' ⍝ In pixels
     yr←arg[1]+0,--/yr ⋄ xr←arg[2]+0,--/xr ⍝ Move origin but keep size
     ⍝? We won't need this, but just to remember what I figured out: yr-←⌊/0,yr ⋄ yr-←⌈/0,yr-pxsize[1] ⋄ xr-←⌊/0,xr ⋄ xr-←⌈/0,xr-pxsize[2] ⍝ Impose range limits
     object ##.##.∆WS('YRange'yr)('XRange'xr)
     result←##.NoRes
 :EndIf
